# Rank 1374 / CVE-2021-21289: mechanize wrote every downloaded body, cookie
# jar and local file through Ruby's bare `open`. `Kernel#open` is a private
# instance method mixed into Object, so a receiverless `open path, mode` is
# `Kernel.open path, mode`, and Ruby documents that method as running the path
# as a subprocess command line when its first character is `|`. The paths
# mechanize passed are not the caller's own constants: `Mechanize::Download`
# and `Mechanize::File` derive @filename from the response's
# Content-Disposition header in extract_filename, and CookieJar#save/#load
# take a path straight from the calling application. A server answering with
# `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="|id"` therefore ran a command on
# the client when the download is saved (CWE-78).
#
# The fixing commit is the PR's content commit; the PR merge's combined diff is empty, so the
# patch is unreadable from the row. The five fixes sit inside it (aae0b13,
# 2ac906b, f43a395, b48b12f, 63f8779) and each replaces the bare call with
# `::File.open`, the spelling that has no pipe behaviour. f43a395,
# "fix(security): prevent command injection in Download#save!", is the readable
# single-commit stand-in for the row.
#
# The weakness class is existing vocabulary: code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution,
# its review twin and VYQL-INJ-042 all exist, and rank 224 covered the explicit
# `Kernel.open` spelling. Only the receiverless spelling — the common one, and
# the one mechanize uses everywhere — has no binding, so the call carries
# code.UrlFetch alone and no pipe-open flag. The new Ruby binding
# matches callee.path exactly, because `~=` is segment-aware in both directions
# and would otherwise pull in `File.open`, `zip.open` and any other
# receiver-qualified `.open` — including the patched form itself.

test "rank1374: a downloaded body saved through bare open can run a piped path"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/mechanize/download.rb
  code
  ```
  class Mechanize::Download
    attr_accessor :filename

    def initialize uri = nil, response = nil, body_io = nil, code = nil
      @uri     = uri
      @body_io = body_io
      fill_header response
      extract_filename
    end

    def save! filename = nil
      filename ||= @filename
      dirname = File.dirname filename
      FileUtils.mkdir_p dirname

      open filename, 'wb' do |io|
        until @body_io.eof? do
          io.write @body_io.read 16384
        end
      end

      filename
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1374: a cookie jar path opened through bare open can run a piped path"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  expect_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/mechanize/cookie_jar.rb
  code
  ```
  class Mechanize::CookieJar < ::HTTP::CookieJar
    def load(input, *options)
      input.respond_to?(:write) or
        return open(input, 'r') { |io| load(io, *options) }

      opthash = {
        :format => :yaml,
        :session => false,
      }
      opthash.update(options.first) if options.first
      opthash
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1374: ::File.open has no pipe behaviour and is not process execution"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/mechanize/download.rb
  code
  ```
  class Mechanize::Download
    attr_accessor :filename

    def initialize uri = nil, response = nil, body_io = nil, code = nil
      @uri     = uri
      @body_io = body_io
      fill_header response
      extract_filename
    end

    def save! filename = nil
      filename ||= @filename
      dirname = File.dirname filename
      FileUtils.mkdir_p dirname

      ::File.open(filename, 'wb') do |io|
        until @body_io.eof? do
          io.write @body_io.read 16384
        end
      end

      filename
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1374: an open method reached through a receiver is not Kernel#open"
  lang ruby
  profile library
  reject_review code.RubyPipeOpenCommandExecution
  file lib/mechanize/http/agent.rb
  code
  ```
  class Mechanize::HTTP::Agent
    def resolve_parameters uri, filename
      File.open(filename, 'rb') { |io| io.read }
      @connection_cache.open(uri.host)
    end
  end
  ```
